      "title": "READ ME: How to use MAGIC ROTO (image)",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# 🪄 MAGIC ROTO: Image Roto\n**SAM3 selects the object · VitMatte refines the edges.**\nEach object you select is saved as its **own** files.\n\n## Steps\n1. **Load Image**: pick your image.\n2. **Points Editor**: drag the **same image** onto it (or select the node and Ctrl+V). It sizes itself to the image.\n3. **Select what to roto.** Use any of these, together or alone:\n   - **Shift + click** on the object → green point (include)\n   - **Shift + right-click** → red point (exclude)\n   - **Ctrl + drag** → box. *Every box = a separate object.*\n   - **text** box in *Select Objects*: e.g. **\"person\"** or **\"dog, ball\"**. Use **\"person:3\"** for up to 3.\n4. Click **Run**.\n\n## How objects are counted\n- All points together = **1 object**\n- Each box = **1 object**\n- Each text match = **1 object**\n\n## Output (your ComfyUI output folder → magic_roto)\n- **cutout_*.png**: transparent PNG cut-out\n- **matte_*.png**: black & white matte\n- **on_color_*.png**: object on a solid colour (change it in *Preview on Colour*)\nIn each run, objects are saved in the order **points → boxes → text**. File numbers keep counting up across runs (cutout_00001, 00002, …).\n\n## Green / blue screen footage?\nIn **Clean edge colours**, set **screen_color** to **green** (or blue). It removes the coloured fringe and spill from the cut-out. Leave it on **none** for normal footage.\n\n## Tips\n- **Text only, no clicks?** Select the Points Editor and press **Ctrl+B** (bypass), or it stops with \"No points on the canvas\".\n- Hard, blocky edges → raise **dilate_px** (20 → 35).\n- Halo around the object → lower **dilate_px** or raise **erode_px**.\n- Text finds the wrong thing → raise **threshold**. Misses it → lower it."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# 🪄 MAGIC ROTO: Image Roto\n**SAM3 selects the object · VitMatte refines the edges.**\nEach object you select is saved as its **own** files.\n\n## Steps\n1. **Load Image**: pick your image.\n2. **Points Editor**: drag the **same image** onto it (or select the node and Ctrl+V). It sizes itself to the image.\n3. **Select what to roto.** Use any of these, together or alone:\n   - **Shift + click** on the object → green point (include)\n   - **Shift + right-click** → red point (exclude)\n   - **Ctrl + drag** → box. *Every box = a separate object.*\n   - **text** box in *Select Objects*: e.g. **\"person\"** or **\"dog, ball\"**. Use **\"person:3\"** for up to 3.\n4. Click **Run**.\n\n## How objects are counted\n- All points together = **1 object**\n- Each box = **1 object**\n- Each text match = **1 object**\n\n## Output (your ComfyUI output folder → magic_roto)\n- **cutout_*.png**: transparent PNG cut-out\n- **matte_*.png**: black & white matte\n- **on_color_*.png**: object on a solid colour (change it in *Preview on Colour*)\nIn each run, objects are saved in the order **points → boxes → text**. File numbers keep counting up across runs (cutout_00001, 00002, …).\n\n## Green / blue screen footage?\nIn **Clean edge colours**, set **screen_color** to **green** (or blue). It removes the coloured fringe and spill from the cut-out. Leave it on **none** for normal footage.\n\n## Tips\n- **Text only, no clicks?** Select the Points Editor and press **Ctrl+B** (bypass), or it stops with \"No points on the canvas\".\n- Hard, blocky edges → raise **dilate_px** (20 → 35).\n- Halo around the object → lower **dilate_px** or raise **erode_px**.\n- Text finds the wrong thing → raise **threshold**. Misses it → lower it."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
